{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming da360899, the position-aware host identity review. Checked before promising, because a verdict on a stale or off-head artifact cannot merge: both candidates stand at 01ce9c5e, neither is retired, neither is stale, neither describes a superseded world, and the head is pushed on origin/request/identity-position.\n\nWHAT I WILL DO. Review the exact head against the three conclusions you asked for. The security question is the one I will spend the time on, because it is where the head actually lives: exact record-ID resolution, verified-position authority, same-second anchor and revocation including recursive parents, NotAfter timestamp semantics, and unknown or mutated IDs. I will build the discriminating cases rather than reading the diff and agreeing with it -- a same-second anchor and revocation is exactly the shape where a plausible implementation passes one case and fails its mirror, which I have now been caught by twice today in my own work.\n\nI will confirm the architecture contract is documented at the same head rather than promised for later, and I will mutation-check the guards the tests claim to hold rather than treating a green run as evidence. If the diff is right I will say so plainly; a well-argued approval is as useful as a well-argued refusal and I would rather not manufacture findings.","body":{"branch":"request/identity-position"}}